comments.body:
if `this` is smaller than `other`, return `greater`?
hmmm, isn't that inverted? Though https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/container/priority_queue.html also uses the largest value having priority, so conceptually it makes sense.
To simplify it slightly, I would either invest it to check for actually use the "greater than" operation:
```C++
    if (other_tie > this_tie) {
        return std::strong_ordering::greater;
```
or since the [CI](https://github.com/l0rinc/bitcoin/actions/runs/19703586332/job/56445553273?pr=58) indicates that if we used the mentioned `NodeSeconds` instead of `NodeClock::time_point` (which is also more reviewer friendly in my opinion), we could simplify this to (preferably in the header):
```C++
auto operator<=>(const Priority& other) const noexcept
{
    return std::tie(other.num_picked, other.num_confirmed, other.last_picked, other.last_confirmed)
       <=> std::tie(num_picked, num_confirmed, last_picked, last_confirmed);
}
```
Note: the CI fails for some of the fuzzers, maybe they need sub-second times? Not sure, haven't checked yet.

