I find the [idiomatic](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/optional.html) way of using `std::optional` to be less repetitive (especially without needing `has_value()` and `.value()`) and that the scope of the variable is reduced - but I won't suggest it anymore if you dislike it:
```suggestion
    if (const auto tx_and_status{GetSendStatusByNode(nodeid)}) {
        return tx_and_status->tx;
    }
```

