Good observation! I think the patch above will resolve it. Note - if the transaction is received back before we close the connection and come here, `Remove()` would already have been called. Then `GetTxForNode()` would return nullopt and no new connections will be requested (correct).

Another option is to drop this `if` from here:

```cpp
if (node.IsPrivateBroadcastConn() && !m_tx_for_private_broadcast.DidNodeConfirmReception(nodeid)) {
    m_connman.m_private_broadcast.NumToOpenAdd(1);
}
```
and then also drop `DidNodeConfirmReception()` because it will be unused. The problem is that in the rare case where the connection does not conclude with `PING` we will not request a new connection to be opened. However this could be compensated with a more aggressive retry of stale transactions - if we take the change from https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/pull/29415#discussion_r2589928992

What to do?

